1. A statue of a grid bug is in a gelatinous cube that is rising at 5
m/s^2. The statue of the grid bug weighs 2 kg. Mu-subS inside the
gelatinous cube is 0.80, and mu-subK inside the cube is 0.50. If the
statue is given a shove of 30 newtons horizontally, will it move?
Assume that the inside of the cube is perfectly level and the statue of
the grid bug is 10 meters away from any side of the cube.

2. A dull spellbook is placed on top of a saddled ki-rin. This surface
is perfectly level. If mu-subS of the surface is 0.50 and the mu-subK
is 0.30, will the spellbook slide if the ki-rin begins accelerating
forward at 5 m/s^2?

3. A trapdoor in the ceiling opens and a rock falls out! The rock is
1kg and the ceiling is 20 meters above the ground. There are 5 newtons
worth of air resistance on the rock. How long does it take for the rock
to hit you if the distance from the bottom of your iron shoes to the
top of your leather hat is 2 meters?

4. The orc-captain shoots a crude arrow! If you are levitating 15
meters off the ground and the arrow hits you in 0.5 seconds, what angle
was the orc-captain shooting at if you were 20 meters away, there is no
air resistance, the orc-captain shot the arrow 1.0 meter above his
feet, and the arrow hits you 1.5 meters above your feet?

5. You hear the rumble of distant thunder! Assuming that gods, who are
the source of the thunder, react instantaneously, and the dungeon's
walls carry sound as well as the dungeon's air, if you killed poor
Bonafido 6 seconds before you hear the thunder, how far away was your
deity?

6. Your pair of speed boots glow violently for a moment, then
vapourize! If all of the mass in the boots were converted to energy,
and the speed boots had a weight of 30 newtons, how much energy was
released?

7. You irradiate yourself with pure energy! If you have magic
resistance, do you still die?

8. You notice that there is no gravity here. If there is also no air
resistance, and you have a mass of 500 kg, how far will you move if you
kick a 3 500 kg orange dragon corpse with a force of 1 000 newtons?

9. The soldier zaps a wand of lightning! If you are 100 meters away
from the soldier, how long does it take for the lightning to reach you,
hit a wall 50 meters behind you, and hit a mastodon 35 meters behind
the soldier?

10. Your sacrifice is consumed in a burst of flame! If the flame lasts
for 10 seconds and is a steady 1000 degrees Celsius, how many litres of
water can it boil?

Assume that the gravity in the dungeon is 10 m/s^2. (It's very close to
the core of the earth.)
Assume that the speed of sound in the dungeon is 340 m/s. (Air works
differently here.)
Assume that the speed of light in the dungeon is 300 000 000 m/s.
(Photons move faster here.)
Assume that the problems below are not 100% perfect and may contain
errors. (I made these up as I went along; tell me what I'm getting
wrong.)
Assume that e=mc^2. (Actually, don't assume.)
Mu-subS represents the coefficient of static friction between two
objects.
Mu-subK represents the coefficient of kinetic friction between two
objects.



